samp=500$, $\dlat=40$, $\pwidth=2560$, $5$ repetitions): bulk mass$/(\sigma_r(
samp-\dlat))=0.9840$ vs $1-\dlat/\pwidth=0.9844$; top edge$/\sigma_r=1.987$ vs $\kappa_{\mathrm{MP}}=2.005$, excluding the additive-model value $(1+\sqrt{\gamma_p})^2=2.079$. Individual outliers fluctuate by $	heta_j\sqrt{2/\pwidth}$, so the per-outlier shift ($\sigma_r$ vs $1.18\sigma_r$) is not resolvable in a single run; (b) is a statement in expectation. In code units the threshold is $	heta_c\pwidth\in[0.03,0.1]$ across the sweep while the smallest noise-dimension eigenvalue is $2$--$5$ at $\signoise=0.5$: every data direction is an outlier by a margin $\ge20	imes$, and the shift $\sigma_r$ is $0.15$--$0.25\%$ of $\lambda^{\mathrm{sig}}_{\min}$ ($a_*^2\pwidth/
samp=0.05$--$0.12$ vs $20$--$74$), which is the operational content of ``the data-side eigenvalues are $\pwidth$-independent'' beyond the $W$ factor of Step~3.

